# TRAVIS APIs Documentation

## Overview

This document lists the external APIs, internal APIs, and communication
protocols used in the TRAVIS (Traffic Violation Recognition and AI
Surveillance) system.

## External APIs


### Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) API

**Purpose:** Push Notifications

Sends real-time push notifications to the mobile application whenever
congestion, traffic violations, collisions, or emergency events are
detected.

## Internal APIs

### start_analysis.php (POST)

Starts the AI analysis by launching the computer vision module to
process the selected video source.

### stop_analysis.php (POST)

Stops the currently running AI analysis and updates the system status.

### get_status.php (GET)

Retrieves the current AI analysis status, processing progress, and
system information.

### update_status.php (POST)

Receives updates from the Python computer vision module and updates the
dashboard status.

### get_monitoring_logs.php (GET)

Retrieves monitoring logs, detected events, and traffic statistics
stored in the database.

### /video_feed (GET - Flask API)

Streams the processed AI video with detection overlays to the monitoring
dashboard in real time.

### predict.php (POST) *(Planned)*

Sends monitoring data to the Machine Learning model and returns
predicted congestion levels.

### mobile/dashboard.php (GET) *(Planned)*

Provides summarized monitoring information for the React Native mobile
application.

### mobile/latest_status.php (GET) *(Planned)*

Returns the latest monitoring status and AI detection results.

### mobile/logs.php (GET) *(Planned)*

Retrieves historical monitoring logs for mobile users.

## Communication Protocol

### RTSP (Real-Time Streaming Protocol)

Used to receive the live video stream from the Tapo Camera.





